									<b><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=812.msg13165#msg13165">Re: people don't need philanthropists, they need power!</a></b>
									<div class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #3 on:</b> January 13, 2007, 04:01:20 pm &#187;</div></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;">I dont believe you are right in that IF the world was perfect and IF wealth was distributed equally then chairty would be unnesessary because the act of doing for those who are in need is a powerfull one.&nbsp; The act of caring for the blind is chairity.&nbsp; Philanthropy is important in what IS a economicly imbalenced world.&nbsp; It is true that most philanthropists gain their money from unethical and oppressive means, but it is better they give some back then none.&nbsp; Imagine if Bill Gates did nothing with his money but save it.&nbsp; What would you say then?&nbsp; How do you cure aids?&nbsp; Inject Mr. Gates with it.&nbsp; How do you stop the genocide in Darfur, drop Gates&#039;s kids off in the middle.</div>
